[Music]  ma can we get rabbits please  the two-year-old me asked my mom with my  eyes gleaming as we returned from the  petting zoo my mom hated rabbits but she  loved me so fast forward two weeks later  I loved my childhood I remember the  clinking sound of my mother's bangles I  she cooked halwa my favorite dessert and  the irresistible smell from the kitchen  that would tell me when the halwa was  ready her kiss on my forehead  when I was sick the power to heal  everything my father was my hero he and  I would watch cricket matches together  every Sunday we would get super absorbed  in the match and I would swear with my  dad as he would swear during the matches  Kyogre da batsman a water dumb batsman  is he  vivir and inseparable duo he was my  cricket coach my college exam tutor my  career counselor I was the little Simba  learning life skills from my father  Mufasa as a kid my parents for my void  then I grew up I became busy with my  college studies attending the parties my  friends through finding the next big job  earning a few extra dollars of bonus  what started as twice-a-day call with my  parents slowly became once a day then  once in two days then once a week my  parents never said a word whenever we  spoke my father would ask beta he cannot  do son are you doing fine he just wanted  me to be happy  I didn't realize what I was missing  until last December  my father had to undergo a major surgery  the doctors could not guarantee a  success and my father was visibly scared  the day before the surgery gave me a  small diary with everything I would need  to know in case something should happen  to him as the day of the surgery arrived  my father lay on the stretcher as the  doctors moved him into the operation  theater as my hand slipped out of my  father's I saw it air roll down his  cheek it was the first time I'd seen my  father cry  I stood there unable to move and the  doors of the operation theater shut  tight in front of me that moment made me  realize that my father my mother was a  human a human who felt fear a human who  felt vulnerability I stood there  wondering why I never had a reciprocal  relationship with my father he knew all  of my stories but I didn't know any  office I thought of all the questions I  wanted to ask my father feelings I  wanted to share and gratitude I wanted  to convey  what if I never got the chance after an  8-hour long surgery the doctors came out  the surgery was successful I could not  hold back my tears up until this moment  I thought I had a deep relationship with  my parents but now realized I didn't  there was so much we never shared what  matters to us what drives us what scares  us  I wanted more I wanted to have a real  honest and emotional relationship with  my parents one we could be honest about  our feelings one maybe could be  ourselves without the fear of  disappointing each other  the only thing I didn't know was how  fortunately after my father surgery this  happened naturally with him seeing each  other's vulnerable side brought us  closer however I struggled to find the  same relationship with my mother she was  immensely loving and caring with her  actions this is the woman who left a  booming career as a banker so that she  could take care of me but she was also  tough and demanding with her words  especially when it came to doing well in  my exams or getting a good job she had  sacrificed so much for me that I've  wanted to be worthy of her efforts my  fear of disappointing her created an  emotional distance between us in an  attempt to close that distance I started  calling her mother every morning we  would talk about what I had for dinner  how are my classes going what happened  in her day during those conversations I  wondered  am i deserving of her love now I didn't  know economists conversations felt  superficial and cosmetic this was in the  relationship I wanted to build  clearly the phone calls weren't working  so I decided to increase my frequency of  visiting home this summer I skipped a  trip with my friends to spend two weeks  back at home I was spending as much time  as I could with her I wondered am i  deserving of her love now no answer  still I didn't know what will make me  worthy of her love and sacrifices I  didn't know what it takes to have a real  relationship I had run out of ideas last  month during one of our usual phone  conversations I decided to simply ask MA  are you proud of me she was surprised  and replied of course I am you're the  best son in the world  I pressed further ma are you proud of me  she replied  give me a minute she returned with a  poem she had written for me when I was 2  she read out the last stanza how can I  ever thank Almighty for this until and  unless I make him a promise I will make  my son a true human being he keeps the  path of truth I shall be seen a true  human being that's all she wanted  her response changed everything for me I  didn't have to jump through all of these  hoops to be worthy of her love I just  had to be a good human being I felt  closer to my mom 7,000 miles away from  home then I ever felt when we went the  same house a relationship with our  parents shapes who we are I have come to  realize that my super type-a personality  was shaped by my desire to be deserving  of my mother's love how might your  relationship with your parents shape you  by being closer to appearance not only  do we create an opportunity to fully see  ourselves but we also create an  opportunity to separate fact from  fiction separate the truth from the  stories we have been making up no matter  where you are in a relationship with  your parents there are more  possibilities don't set up a few months  earlier I would have said I have a deep  relationship with my parents but now I  know so much more was and still is  possible some  building a real relationship just  require starting with a question my  question was are you proud of me  what will your question be thank you  [Applause]  [Music]

